# Deployment-specific names that must never appear in shipped source.
#
# Copy to .appsec-forbidden (gitignored) and fill in the identifiers belonging
# to this deployment: the GitHub org and enterprise slug, the Renovate bot's
# login, admin usernames, the AWS account alias. One per line, matched
# case-insensitively as a regular expression against every .ts/.tsx file.
#
# This file stays empty of real values so it can be committed. The list itself
# is deliberately kept out of git: writing the names down in the repository is
# the thing the check exists to prevent. APPSEC_FORBIDDEN, a comma-separated
# environment variable, does the same job in CI without a file on disk.
#
# Identifiers with a recognizable shape — AWS account ids, GitHub App client
# ids, tokens, private keys — are matched without configuration and need no
# entry here.
